[Music]  hi  i'm jennifer and today i'm joined by  leslie from globe telecom to discuss how  they leverage google cloud's no code  platform  app sheet to empower citizen developers  leslie thank you so much for joining us  hi jennifer thank you for having me here  absolutely  all right so first question for you why  no code technology  so we introduced no code platform  because there are a lot of good  ideas that never really get into the  pipeline due to failed business case  limited project resources or just by  mere intimidation of  justifying that initiative so we see  that a no code platform can provide an  alternative path  for business process automation in  delivering applications without being  subjected to requirements  or the constraints of the standard  development process  so the smes or the end users are  able to solve their own pain points or  problems through the no code application  that's fantastic so what problems does  appsheet solve for you app sheet enables  the development of  niche applications so these are  applications that are used for specific  process  and groups in the organization  individually  they may not provide enough value to  merit building an  application in the traditional way but  these niche  applications are in the long tail and  the combined value is comparable  with the value delivered by our big or  in complex applications  so with app sheet we are able to allow  employees to automate their  own process without the need of a  developer or worrying about much of the  cost  either they find it time-consuming to  report on a service vehicle usage  or when they're on site just doing  simple data gathering  so these are issues that our frontliners  face but  never really get resolved before so  frontliners i'm definitely borrowing  that word but that aside  it sounds like working with this  platform has helped a number  address a number of the problems within  your organization but how has this  product changed how you work  so jennifer we just introduced app sheet  in our company around four months ago  and the result has been very impressive  so we conducted a no  code hackathon program as our adoption  strategy  so we invited all our employees to join  we conducted workshops  then we gave them eight weeks to  complete their application and that's on  top of their usual workload  now we saw a number of simple issues  that we didn't know still  exist and employees with no coding  background were able to  complete and build a working solution  with immediate results  now a lot of employees are reaching out  to us to learn more about app sheet  so as an example currently we are on  budgeting season  and our finance guys reach out to us to  to build an application using app sheet  so they were able to streamline the  budgeting process by just using this  platform and now when we introduce  a new process or looking into improving  our existing process  it is becoming a norm to consider app  sheet for process automation  that's amazing so what actions  have you taken to help your organization  adopt unicode technology  all right so the success of the no code  hackathon made a very good  impact in showcasing our employees the  winners  and the applications they built using  app sheet  we believe we were able to get those  early adopters  to get their insights and support for  our program  from there we also started our own globe  app sheet community  to keep that momentum going after the  buzz from the hackathon  and to increase more traction we  included  app sheet as a course in our globe  university  our globe university leads the learning  and development  across all our globe business units so  we also include some prerequisite  courses to understand the process  improvement  and basic user experience our employees  should be able to identify the overall  benefits  of the solution or application that they  plan to build  okay one last question for you leslie  since it sounds like you're ahead of the  curve when it comes to no code  technology  why should others consider adopting that  same type of technology  all right so the no code platform is not  a replacement of our software  development team  we still need to continue to create big  and complex applications to serve our  customers  and we still definitely need our it  developer  for these but there are applications in  the long tail  that are often ignored or deprioritized  so we believe that the no code platform  is the solution for those  combined with it governance no code  platform  will help speed your digital  transformation by enabling your  employees to become citizen developers  your company can solve pain points in  your process that are never elevated to  the top management  not just that the employees will also be  motivated as we empower them to create  their own applications  well leslie thank you so much for taking  the time to join us and tell your story  and for those interested in learning  more about how google cloud's no code  technology app sheet can help empower  citizen developers like you  check out the details below  you

